Subject: [PATCH 11/15] feat(surface-placement-audit): snap and tangent
 controls, review fixes

Two controls on the offsets: each located peak is remeasured after snapping
the point to it (precision of the peak location), and a second point 2, 4 and
8 voxels away in the tangent plane is measured (scale over which the offset is
a property of the surface). Patch ids are 32-voxel cells, since obj vertices
are not in grid order.

Review fixes: HTTP range reads need status 206 and time out; the obj handle is
closed; parsed vertices must be three finite floats; a 4D volume is indexed on
its last three axes; a NaN metric fails --fail-on; the fail-on parser is
shared with the topology audit through a keys argument.

On three public Scroll 1 segments the snap control spreads 0.4 voxels and the
tangent offsets agree at 2 and 4 voxels but not at 8, so the flat offset
histogram (half the surface more than 2 voxels from the sheet) is a mesh
resolution limit, not drift. Documented.
